      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we will utilize the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\).\n\nFirst, apply the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(235 - 221\\):\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(235 + 221\\):\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nNow substitute these values back into the expression:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n\\]\n\nNext, perform the multiplication \\(14 \\times 456\\):\n\\[\n14 \\times 456 = 14 \\times (400 + 50 + 6) = 14 \\times 400 + 14 \\times 50 + 14 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term separately:\n\\[\n14 \\times 400 = 5600\n\\]\n\\[\n14 \\times 50 = 700\n\\]\n\\[\n14 \\times 6 = 84\n\\]\n\nAdd these results together:\n\\[\n5600 + 700 + 84 = 6384\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute this result back into the original expression:\n\\[\n\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14} = \\frac{6384}{14}\n\\]\n\nFinally, perform the division:\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of the given expression is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{456}\n\\]",
