      "text": "The expression can be simplified as follows:\n\n$$\\frac{235^2-221^2}{14}=\\frac{(235+221)(235-221)}{14}=\\frac{456 \\times 14}{14}=\\boxed{456}$$\nFind: $\\displaystyle\\frac{199^2-193^2}{21}=$\n\nTo solve the expression \\(\\frac{199^2 - 193^2}{21}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 199\\) and \\(b = 193\\). Applying the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n199^2 - 193^2 = (199 - 193)(199 + 193)\n\\]\n\nCalculating the terms inside the parentheses:\n\n\\[\n199 - 193 = 6\n\\]\n\\[\n199 + 193 = 392\n\\]\n\nSo, the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n199^2 - 193^2 = 6 \\times 392 = 2352\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to divide this result by 21:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2352}{21} = 112\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\frac{199^2 - 193^2}{21}\\) is \\(\\boxed{112}\\).",
